  30:     - The only other non-background color appears as isolated source pixels scattered on either side of the guide.
  31: 
  32:     Rule
  33:     - Start from an otherwise empty background canvas and keep the guide bar fixed.
  34:     - If the guide is horizontal, each source pixel whose column contains a guide pixel moves to the row directly above or below that guide pixel, preserving its side of the guide.
  35:     - If the guide is vertical, each source pixel whose row contains a guide pixel moves to the column directly left or right of that guide pixel, preserving its side of the guide.
  36:     - Source pixels whose perpendicular projection would hit a gap in the guide are erased.
  37: 
  38:     Key insight
  39:     - The guide bar defines the valid landing slots; the scattered pixels are not copied in place, but compressed along perpendicular sightlines to the nearest cells beside that guide.
